<h1>Can I use AI to write my will in Michigan?</h1>
<p>An AI-drafted estate plan can look polished and still fail when your family needs it. Here is where it goes wrong, and what a Michigan attorney catches that a chatbot cannot.</p>
<div class="meta">Pascaris Law Firm, PLLC &nbsp;|&nbsp; Estate planning &nbsp;|&nbsp; 5 minute read</div>
</div>
<div class="sheet" aria-hidden="true">
<h2>Last Will and Testament</h2>
<div class="ln">I, being of sound mind, declare this</div>
<div class="ln">to be my will. I name <mark>[state not checked]</mark></div>
<div class="ln">as personal representative and direct</div>
<div class="ln">that my estate pass to <mark>[unfunded trust]</mark></div>
<div class="ln">Signed before <mark>[witnesses unverified]</mark></div>
<div class="note">Looks finished. Not yet effective.</div>
</div>
</div></section>

